@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Prioritize a story across epics
actor "Authorized user" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "BacklogView, or MovePositionDialog / MovePositionForm" as page
  participant "IWorkOrderService / WorkOrderService" as client
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "WorkOrdersController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ValidationBehavior" as validation
  participant "PrioritizeStoryCommandHandler" as handler
  participant "WorkOrder" as entity
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box
actor -> page : Drag within the page, Move up / Move down, or Move to position...
page -> page : BacklogView snapshots its saved page; compute the absolute target rank (rank 26 up becomes 25 on page 1); one move at a time, never debounced
page -> client : prioritize(PrioritizeStoryCommand: story, absolute target position, expected backlog-order version from BacklogItemPage.orderVersion, carried in MoveTarget for the dialog)
client -> access : PUT /api/workspaces/{id}/work-order/backlog
access -> access : L2-002 validate signature, issuer, audience, subject, expiry
access -> db : Read current status, role and credential version
db --> access : Current account access
alt Missing, invalid or expired JWT; deactivated account
  access --> client : 401; audit denial without payloads
  client --> page : sessionInterceptor calls SessionService.end(Unauthorized) once for this generation; the promise rejects with its 401 (nothing written); restore snapshot; sign-in shows session-unsaved when a draft was dirty, then returns to the backlog
else Authenticated active account (profile P: prioritizing needs no capability beyond an active session)
  access -> ctrl : Authorized request
  ctrl -> validation : Send PrioritizeStoryCommand through MediatR 12.5.0
  validation -> validation : Identifiers well formed; target position is a whole number of 1 or more
  alt Malformed request
    validation --> ctrl : 400 field errors; nothing read or changed
    ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
    client --> page : Restore snapshot; MovePositionDialog keeps the value and focus moves to the position field, which reads its message; no Retry or reference ID
  else Valid request
    validation -> handler : Handle PrioritizeStoryCommand
    handler -> db : BeginWorkspaceTransactionAsync takes the workspace lock first; LoadBacklogOrderAsync loads the tracked story backlog order, its count, and its version
    db --> handler : Ordered story IDs and version, or lock-wait timeout
    alt Workspace lock wait times out
      handler --> ctrl : 503 with Retry-After; nothing read or changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (unavailable)
      client --> page : Unavailable save: restore snapshot; highlight the story; Try again resends the same move only when chosen (reorder-failed state)
    else Workspace or story not found
      handler --> ctrl : 404; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not found)
      client --> page : BacklogView rereads the page without the story and announces that it no longer exists; after a drag or Move up or Move down the focused row is gone, so focus moves to the row now at that rank, or to the backlog heading when no row is left there; an open dialog closes with NotFound, and BacklogPage increments its refresh counter and shows the toast
    else Story from another workspace, not a story, or position beyond the full count (L2-017.3)
      handler --> ctrl : 400 invalid position or reference; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
      client --> page : Restore snapshot; the dialog shows "Enter a position from 1 to N" with focus on the position field (out-of-range state); an inline move shows the reason with Reload backlog, without Try again or a reference ID
    else Stale backlog-order version (L2-041)
      handler --> ctrl : 409 order changed; nothing applied
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (order changed)
      client --> page : Restore snapshot; highlight the story; never resent. "Backlog order changed" alert announced without moving focus, because the move controls stay enabled; Reload backlog only, which rereads the page and returns focus to the story's row (reorder-conflict state). Dialog: Reload order receives focus and closes it with Outdated
    else Move permitted
      handler -> entity : L2-017 move the story in the backlog only
      entity --> handler : New priority interval; parents, sibling order, board order, and sprint membership unchanged
      handler -> db : L2-039 / L2-040 AddAuditEvent, then SaveChangesAsync: rewrite the affected interval, bump the backlog-order version, and record success audit in one transaction; release the lock
      alt Commit fails
        db --> handler : Roll back business state and success audit
        handler --> ctrl : Generic 500 with correlation ID
        ctrl --> client : Failure; no successful-move claim
        client --> page : Restore snapshot; highlight the story; keep focus on the move control; Try again resends the same move (reorder-failed state)
      else Commit succeeds
        db --> handler : New backlog-order version
        handler --> ctrl : Committed rank
        ctrl --> client : 200 OrderMoved (rank, total, order version)
        client --> page : BacklogView rereads the page holding the new rank, following the story across a page boundary; that page becomes the saved snapshot. After Move to position the dialog closes with Moved; BacklogPage increments its refresh counter and passes the result to revealMoved, which does the same
        page --> actor : Announce "Moved {title} to position N of M"; focus stays on the move control, or moves to the story's row when it landed on another page
      end
    end
  end
end
opt No response to the move (timeout or network failure)
  client --> page : The move may have committed. Inline: BacklogView rereads the page and the reorder-failed alert says "We couldn't confirm whether {title} moved" and where the reread found it, without a reference ID or Try again. Dialog: the failed alert with that title and no reference ID; the form emits unconfirmed, so BacklogPage rereads at once; Try again resends only when pressed, and a 409 to that resend drops "Nothing was applied" and says to reload to see where the story is now
end
note over ctrl, db
An unexpected 403 applies nothing; BacklogView restores its snapshot (or MovePositionForm keeps the position) and emits forbidden, and the routed page shows the "Your access changed" toast through TOAST_SERVICE, without Retry or reference ID; the capability refresh still runs.
All rejection checks run under the lock before any write; a stale version in SaveChangesAsync raises ConcurrencyConflictException, the same 409.
Unexpected failures return generic 500 plus correlation ID (L2-043).
Diagnostics exclude secrets and contact payloads.
end note
@enduml
